// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// T27 OS pty_server: the long-lived process that owns one pseudo-terminal per pane, so an agent CLI
// (Claude Code, Codex, a shell) keeps running when the window closes or crashes (the herdr.dev model).
// It spawns the pane's command in the pane's cwd, keeps a 64 KiB scrollback ring per pane, serves the
// frames of pty_proto.t27 on ~/.t27os/pty.sock, and writes one record per pane under ~/.t27os/sessions
// (session_store.t27) on every change. When the server dies, its masters close, the panes get SIGHUP, and
// the next start reads the records and brings every pane back by the agents.t27 RESUME_* rules.
//
// One binary, three modes, picked by the environment so no argv parsing is needed:
//   (none)             serve
//   T27OS_HOOK=1       a Claude Code hook: read the payload on stdin, forward it as OP_HOOK to pane
//                      T27OS_PANE, exit. The server writes ~/.t27os/hooks.json so claude panes run it.
